    "content": "# The Johor Bahru–Singapore RTS Link: What It Changes for Property\n\nThe Rapid Transit System Link is a rail line across the Straits of Johor connecting Bukit Chagar in Johor Bahru with Woodlands North in Singapore. For anyone thinking about property in JB, it is the single most important piece of infrastructure to understand — not because of what marketing says it will do to prices, but because of what it does to a daily commute.\n\nThis guide sticks to what has been published about the line and to how I would use it when choosing a project. The opening date and capacity figures below are the project's own announced ones; confirm them against the operators' latest statements before you rely on them.\n\n---\n\n## 1. What the line is\n\n- **Two stations.** Bukit Chagar on the Johor side, Woodlands North on the Singapore side, where it meets the Thomson–East Coast Line.\n- **A few minutes station to station.** The journey itself is short. The time that matters is the whole trip, door to door, and that depends on how you reach Bukit Chagar.\n- **Immigration cleared once.** Both countries' immigration is co-located, so you clear at departure and walk out at the other end. This is the part that changes daily commuting: it removes the queue, not just the distance.\n- **Capacity.** The line is designed for around 10,000 passengers an hour in each direction, according to the project's published figures.\n- **Opening.** Officially scheduled for the end of 2026. Until it opens, treat it as a plan.\n\n---\n\n## 2. What it does to property — and what it does not\n\nThe honest answer is that the RTS makes living in JB and working in Singapore practical for people who would not have done it while the Causeway was the only way across. That expands the pool of tenants and owner-occupiers for homes within easy reach of Bukit Chagar. It does not, on its own, make every project in Johor a good buy.\n\nTwo things I watch for:\n\n- **Reach to the station, measured honestly.** \"Near the RTS\" in a brochure can mean a 25-minute walk in Malaysian heat. Ask for the distance in metres, and whether there is a covered route.\n- **Supply.** Johor built a great deal of high-rise stock in the last decade. Demand from the RTS meets that stock; it does not erase it. A building in the right place with a sensible unit count will do better than a large one that happens to be inside the radius.\n\nI do not publish price-per-square-foot histories or yield forecasts for the corridor. The figures that circulate online are not from any source I can verify, and a number I cannot stand behind does not belong on this page.\n\n---\n\n## 3. The zones, by distance to the station\n\n**Bukit Chagar and JB Sentral — the core.** Within walking distance of the station and the CIQ. This is where the commuting case is strongest and where land is scarcest.\n\n**Tanjung Puteri and the waterfront — 1 to 2.5 km.** R&F Princess Cove sits here; the developer describes a covered pedestrian link towards the JB Sentral side, which matters in the rain. I have the project on [propertyportal.my](https://www.propertyportal.my) with its measured distances.\n\n**Larkin and beyond — 3 km and out.** Cheaper entry, but the RTS is a drive or a bus away, which is a different proposition from walking.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Before you buy in the corridor\n\n1. **Developer track record.** Who built it, what they have completed, and whether the project is under the Housing Development Act.\n2. **Management.** For a completed building, ask for the accounts: collection rate and sinking fund balance. A coastal high-rise needs upkeep, and a management body that cannot collect fees cannot provide it.\n3. **Access by road.** The station is one exit; the car park ramp and the surrounding roads at 7am are the rest of your life.\n4. **The rules for foreign buyers.** Johor's minimum purchase price for foreigners, and the lower entry in its designated zones, are in my [foreign buyer guide](/blog/foreigner-buying-property-in-malaysia). State consent and RPGT apply as everywhere else.\n\n---\n\nI am Shyan Yee, REN 46305, IQI Realty. If you want the JB projects I cover listed by measured distance to Bukit Chagar, message me on WhatsApp.",
